1
00:00:00,333 --> 00:00:04,343
Four and a half thousand years ago,
a city had drains in every street.

2
00:00:04,574 --> 00:00:07,064
It was part of the Indus
Valley Civilization.

3
00:00:07,354 --> 00:00:09,194
From about 2600 BC,

4
00:00:09,194 --> 00:00:13,544
it spread across what is now
Pakistan and north-west India.

5
00:00:13,825 --> 00:00:16,075
Its two great cities were Harappa and

6
00:00:16,445 --> 00:00:17,355
Mohenjo-daro.

7
00:00:17,596 --> 00:00:20,986
Their streets ran in neat grids,
crossing at right angles.

8
00:00:21,272 --> 00:00:24,522
Houses were built of baked brick,
all in the same size.

9
00:00:24,782 --> 00:00:28,632
Many had their own bathroom,
and drains that carried the water away.

10
00:00:28,893 --> 00:00:33,163
At Mohenjo-daro stood a great public bath,
made watertight with tar.

11
00:00:33,514 --> 00:00:36,544
Traders used stone weights
that matched from city to city.

12
00:00:36,794 --> 00:00:40,884
They sailed to far places,
and a dockyard has been found at Lothal.

13
00:00:41,035 --> 00:00:44,665
They carved small stone seals
with animals and strange signs.

14
00:00:45,066 --> 00:00:47,376
No one has been able to read that script.

15
00:00:47,637 --> 00:00:48,767
It is still a mystery.

16
00:00:49,127 --> 00:00:52,617
Around 1900 BC, the cities slowly emptied.

17
00:00:52,988 --> 00:00:55,598
Maybe the climate changed,
or the rivers shifted.

18
00:00:55,874 --> 00:00:57,124
We still debate it.

19
00:00:57,334 --> 00:01:00,524
Then the cities were forgotten
for almost four thousand years.

20
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:04,310
In the 1920s,
archaeologists dug them out again.

21
00:01:04,611 --> 00:01:08,581
They found a civilization older
than almost any city in the world.

